# ============================================
# KrushiLink — Cursor AI Rules
# B2B Agricultural Supply Chain Platform
# Sri Lanka | 2025
# ============================================

## Project Overview
KrushiLink is a multi-tenant B2B SaaS platform that connects
farmers and agricultural suppliers directly with retailers,
supermarkets, and restaurants in Sri Lanka — eliminating
middlemen and reducing post-harvest waste.

## User Roles
- farmer: Lists harvest availability, receives orders via SMS
- retailer: Browses listings, joins demand pools, pays digitally
- admin: Monitors platform, manages disputes, views analytics
- logistics: Receives delivery manifests, confirms deliveries

## Core Business Logic
- Farmers list crops 3-5 days before harvest with quantity and price
- Retailers pool orders together to meet farmer minimum order quantities
- Platform auto-closes pools and generates logistics manifests
- Escrow payments: held on order, released on confirmed delivery
- Farmers receive SMS alerts (not push) — many use basic phones

## Tech Stack

### Frontend
- Framework: Next.js 14 with App Router
- Language: TypeScript strict mode always
- Styling: Tailwind CSS
- State: React hooks + Supabase realtime
- Forms: react-hook-form + zod validation

### Backend
- Database: Supabase (PostgreSQL)
- Auth: Supabase Auth with JWT roles
- RLS: Row-Level Security always enabled
- API: Next.js API routes + Supabase server client
- Payments: PayHere gateway (LKR, Sri Lanka)
- SMS: Dialog Axiata API (primary), Twilio (fallback)
- Maps: Google Maps Distance Matrix API
- Mobile: React Native + Expo (farmer app)

## Folder Structure
src/app/(auth)/           # login, register
src/app/(farmer)/         # farmer portal
src/app/(retailer)/       # retailer portal
src/app/(admin)/          # admin portal
src/app/(logistics)/      # logistics portal
src/app/api/              # API routes
src/components/ui/        # reusable components
src/lib/supabase/         # supabase client instances
src/lib/validations/      # zod schemas
src/lib/types/            # TypeScript types
src/hooks/                # custom React hooks

## Database Tables
- users: id, role, full_name, phone, district, verified_at
- farms: id, owner_id, name, location_lat, location_lng, district, crop_types[]
- harvest_listings: id, farm_id, crop_name, quantity_kg, base_price_lkr,
  available_from, available_until, status, created_at
- demand_pools: id, listing_id, district, closes_at,
  total_committed_kg, moq_kg, status
- pool_orders: id, pool_id, retailer_id, quantity_kg,
  confirmed_at, payment_status
- deliveries: id, pool_id, logistics_provider_id,
  route_manifest (JSONB), scheduled_at, completed_at
- transactions: id, pool_order_id, amount_lkr,
  platform_fee_lkr, payout_status, payhere_reference
- notifications: id, user_id, channel, message, sent_at

## Code Rules
- TypeScript strict mode always, never use 'any'
- Functional components only, prefer Server Components
- snake_case for DB columns, camelCase for TS variables
- PascalCase for components, kebab-case for routes
- Always validate inputs with Zod before DB operations
- Never expose service_role key on the client side
- Always handle Supabase errors explicitly
- Check user role server-side before any data mutation
- Write comments explaining business logic (why, not what)